NODE_ENV=development
# Development: 0.0.0.0:3101 so the app is reachable on http://192.168.1.10:3101
# Production:  127.0.0.1:3100 behind nginx (home.example.be)
PORT=3101
HOST=0.0.0.0
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wickedhome:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/wickedhome_dev
# true once served over https; false while testing on http://192.168.1.10
COOKIE_SECURE=false
# Public address of the app: the OAuth issuer and the MCP resource for ChatGPT/Claude connectors
# (ai/docs/MCP-OAUTH.md). Default https://home.example.be.
# Required in production: the app's public address. The Google redirect, the push contact and the
# dev server's allowed host all derive from it.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://home.example.be
SESSION_DAYS=30
# Uploaded documents live here, outside the code (create the folder, owned by the app user)
STORAGE_DIR=/var/www/wickedhome-data/files
# Largest document upload in MB (decimal); keep nginx client_max_body_size in step
MAX_UPLOAD_MB=100
# Weather: optional Google Maps Platform API key with the Weather API enabled (billing required).
# Without it, "Google" shows as "not configured" in Settings. Never exposed to the browser.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Integrations: key that encrypts per-user tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM, 32 bytes base64).
# Generate once with: openssl rand -base64 32   (changing it later means everyone reconnects)
# INTEGRATIONS_KEY=
# Google per user (Calendar, Gmail bill suggestions, Drive): OAuth client "Web application" in Google Cloud.
# See docs/INTEGRATIONS.md ("Google as built") for the setup steps. Without both, Google shows "not configured".
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional; must equal the Authorised redirect URI of the OAuth client.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://home.example.be/api/integrations/google/callback
# Home Assistant (devices, energy statistics, Verisure alarm). Base URL on the LAN and a long-lived access token
# (Home Assistant -> your profile -> Security -> Long-lived access tokens). Never exposed to the browser.
# See docs/INTEGRATIONS.md ("Home Assistant as built"). Without both, Home Assistant shows "not configured".
# HOME_ASSISTANT_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8123
# HOME_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
# Only when the database holds more than one household: the one Home Assistant belongs to.
# HOME_ASSISTANT_HOUSEHOLD_ID=
# Assistant (ai/docs/ASSISTANT.md): LM Studio on a LAN PC with "Serve on Local Network" on, and the model's
# identifier as LM Studio shows it (a model with tool support, e.g. a Qwen 3 model). Without both, the
# assistant shows "not configured".
# ASSISTANT_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:1234/v1
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=qwen3-27b
# Only if the model server asks for a key (LM Studio: Developer → Settings → require an API token); sent as
# "Authorization: Bearer …". ASSISTANT_TOKEN is the same setting under another name.
# ASSISTANT_API_KEY=
# ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
# Let the model reason before answering (slower); default off.
# ASSISTANT_THINKING=on
# Images in questions (attach button in the chat), sent to the model as image parts. Needs a model with
# image support (Gemma 4, Qwen-VL…); set off for a text-only model. Default on.
# ASSISTANT_VISION=off
# Log the prompt size of every model call in production too (always logged in development).
# ASSISTANT_LOG_TOKENS=1
# Model call limits in seconds: until the answer starts (prompt reading included; a slow PC needs more),
# silence mid-answer, and the whole call (empty = no limit).
# ASSISTANT_TIMEOUT_FIRST_BYTE=300
# ASSISTANT_TIMEOUT_IDLE=60
# ASSISTANT_TIMEOUT_TOTAL=
# Model calls at once (default 1). Keep it equal to LM Studio's "Max Concurrent Predictions": more calls queue in
# the app (chats before the mail scan), so two prompts never fill the GPU at the same time.
# ASSISTANT_PARALLEL=1
# Optional voice: a local Whisper server with an OpenAI-compatible /audio/transcriptions endpoint.
# ASSISTANT_STT_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8000/v1
# ASSISTANT_STT_MODEL=whisper-1
# Optional natural voice for reading answers aloud (ai/docs/ASSISTANT.md "Speech output"): Piper's HTTP server on
# this machine (pm2 wickedhome-tts). Without it the browser's own voice reads. KIND is piper (default) or openai
# (an OpenAI-compatible /audio/speech server; give the URL with /v1; MODEL is for that kind only).
# ASSISTANT_TTS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5005
# ASSISTANT_TTS_KIND=piper
# ASSISTANT_TTS_VOICE_NL=nl_BE-nathalie-medium
# ASSISTANT_TTS_VOICE_EN=en_GB-alba-medium
# ASSISTANT_TTS_SPEED=1
# ASSISTANT_TTS_MODEL=tts-1
# Optional web search for the assistant (ai/docs/WEB-SEARCH.md): the self-hosted SearXNG on this machine
# (pm2 wickedhome-search, JSON output on). Without it the web skill isn't offered. LANGUAGE defaults to nl-BE.
# SEARCH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888
# SEARCH_LANGUAGE=nl-BE
